# AutoCAD dialects: OPEN's file encoding diverges from AutoCAD 2022 at LISPSYS 1 / 2

Status: TODO
Priority: P2
Found: 2026-10-06, E1 (encoding:experiment:lispsys-bom:autocad:windows, job
16980926802, MR !438): AutoCAD 2022 accoreconsole (ACADVER 24.1), LISPSYS set
to 0, 1, 2 in every profile and the engine restarted at each level.

## Measured

Writing "A" e-acute "B" (3 characters) and reading it back:

| LISPSYS | (open f "w") | (open f "w" "utf8") | (open f "w" "utf8-bom") |
|---------+--------------+---------------------+--------------------------|
| 0       | 3 B, cp1252  | ERR too many args   | ERR too many args        |
| 1, 2    | 3 B, cp1252  | 4 B, UTF-8 no BOM   | 7 B, UTF-8 with BOM      |

| LISPSYS | read (open f "r")                    | read (open f "r" "utf8")                     |
|---------+--------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------|
| 0       | cp1252 file -> (65 233 66)           | ERR too many args                            |
| 1, 2    | cp1252, UTF-8 and UTF-8+BOM files    | UTF-8 file -> (65 233 66);                   |
|         | ALL read back (65 233 66)            | UTF-8+BOM -> (65279 65 233 66) (BOM is read  |
|         |                                      | as a character); cp1252 file -> (65): stops  |
|         |                                      | at the invalid byte                          |

And (load) at LISPSYS 1 / 2 reads a cp1252, a UTF-8 and a UTF-8+BOM source
all as 3 characters (at 0: UTF-8 without decoding).

## Divergences in clautolisp (AutoCAD dialects)

1. The default WRITE encoding: clautolisp makes it UTF-8 at LISPSYS 1 / 2
   (%autocad-default-file-encoding, transmit.lisp, used for LOAD and OPEN);
   AutoCAD 2022 keeps writing cp1252 at every level. LISPSYS governs LOAD /
   the default READ, not OPEN's default WRITE.
2. "utf8-bom" writes no BOM in clautolisp; AutoCAD writes EF BB BF.
3. (open f "r" "utf8"): AutoCAD returns the BOM as U+FEFF and stops at the
   first byte that is not UTF-8; clautolisp decodes leniently.
4. (open f "r") at LISPSYS 1 / 2 decodes cp1252 and UTF-8 alike -- check that
   clautolisp's read default under the AutoCAD dialects does the same (it
   decodes per *AUTOLISP-FILE-ENCODING*).

## To do

Implement per the AutoCAD dialects (dialect-version rule: AutoCAD 2021+ has
LISPSYS), with tests from the table above; leave BricsCAD and the clautolisp
dialects as they are (BricsCAD measured separately, probe-open-encoding).
